# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# React Router uses history mode, so a hard load of /dashboard or /admin asks
# the static host for a file that does not exist. Without this rule the host
# returns its own 404 and the app never boots — which looks identical to a
# broken deployment.
#
# API calls are NOT proxied here. The client talks to the API directly via
# REACT_APP_API_URL, and the server sets CORS headers to allow it.
/*    /index.html   200
